@startuml
!theme plain
|a_default| Default
|a_default|
start
:To start the process, begin by checking if the order has been received.;
:v1: sum of the order ({less than 500, greater than 2000, 1000 to 1500, 500 to 999}); <<objectSignal>>
switch ()
case ([v1 = 'less than 500'])
:If the sum of the order is less than 500;
:is less than 500;
:continue with the process;
:if it is still less than 500;
:is still less than 500;
case ([v1 = 'greater than 2000'])
:if the sum of the order is greater than 2000;
:is greater than 2000;
:compute a discount of 4%;
:If the sum of the order is greater than 2000;
case ([v1 = '1000 to 1500'])
:If the sum of the order falls between 1000 and 1500;
:falls between 1000 and 1500;
:compute a discount of 3%;
case ([v1 = '500 to 999'])
:if the sum of the order falls between 500 and 999;
:falls between 500 and 999;
:compute a discount of 2%;
endswitch
:Once again, check the sum of the order.;
:If it is less than 500, continue with the process. If the sum of the order falls between 1000 and 1500, compute a discount of 3%. Likewise, if the sum of the order falls between 500 and 999, compute a discount of 2%.;
:Finally, create the bill;
:and the process will come to an end.;
stop
@enduml